            {
              "text": "When navigating separation, property settlement, or parenting disputes on Brisbane’s Southside, you have access to a mix of long-established community solicitors, dispute resolution experts, and multilingual boutique firms. \n\nA curated shortlist of reputable law firms in and immediately adjacent to **Mount Gravatt** and **Sunnybank**, along with the reasons to consider them, includes:\n\n---\n\n### 1. Wheldon & Associates (Sunnybank)\n* **Location:** 12 Zamia Street, Sunnybank  \n* **Key Areas:** Divorce, property settlements, binding financial agreements (BFAs), parenting arrangements, and domestic violence orders (DVOs).  \n* **Why Choose Them:**\n  * **Established Local Track Record:** A stalwart on the Southside legal scene for decades, known for offering down-to-earth, transparent advice.\n  * **Cost-Conscious Approach:** They place a strong emphasis on early out-of-court resolutions, helping clients avoid unnecessary, financially draining litigation.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Ian W. Bartels & Associates (Mount Gravatt)\n* **Location:** Logan Road & Selborne Street, Mount Gravatt  \n* **Key Areas:** De facto separations, marital divorce, property distribution, parenting disputes, and DVO representation.  \n* **Why Choose Them:**\n  * **Senior Experience:** Principal Ian Bartels has over 30 years of legal experience in Queensland. \n  * **Continuity of Care:** Unlike larger firms where files may be passed down to rotating junior solicitors, they operate as a close-knit practice where your matter is handled directly by an experienced practitioner from start to finish.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Madsen Law (Sunnybank & Southside)\n* **Location:** Sunnybank office (with Southside/Logan integration)  \n* **Key Areas:** Complex asset divisions, child custody/parenting agreements, divorce, and mediation.  \n* **Why Choose Them:**\n  * **Family Law Focus:** Madsen Law has built a notable reputation across the Brisbane South and Logan corridors specifically for family law advocacy.\n  * **Empathetic yet Tough Advocacy:** They are well-regarded for navigating high-conflict parenting disputes and contentious financial settlements while striving for mediated outcomes first.\n\n---\n\n### 4. Bennett Carroll Solicitors (Upper Mount Gravatt)\n* **Location:** Upper Mount Gravatt  \n* **Key Areas:** Separation, child access/custody, property transfers, and commercial/business settlement structuring.  \n* **Why Choose Them:**\n  * **Multidisciplinary Capability:** When a family separation intersects with family businesses, commercial trusts, or complex property portfolios, Bennett Carroll's broader commercial and property divisions allow for seamless cross-disciplinary handling.\n  * **Modern, Practical Guidance:** Known for structured, transparent billing and pragmatic legal roadmaps.\n\n---\n\n### 5. Denovo Lawyers (Sunnybank Hills)\n* **Location:** Sunnybank Hills  \n* **Key Areas:** Separation agreements, property distribution, parenting plans, and family violence matters.  \n* **Why Choose Them:**\n  * **Multilingual & Culturally Aware:** Sunnybank is culturally diverse; Denovo provides legal services with strong cross-cultural competency and language support.\n  * **Boutique Personal Service:** They take a client-first, accessible approach suited to individuals wanting direct, approachable communication rather than stiff corporate overhead.\n\n---\n\n### 6. Campbells Legal (Upper Mount Gravatt)\n* **Location:** Upper Mount Gravatt  \n* **Key Areas:** Separation, parenting, property agreements, estate planning post-divorce.  \n* **Why Choose Them:**\n  * **Generational Trust:** A family-run practice led by solicitors with decades of combined Queensland experience.\n  * **Bespoke Focus:** Ideal for clients seeking low-stress, sensible counsel where direct solicitor access and longstanding Southside community familiarity matter.\n\n---\n\n### Tips for Choosing the Right Family Lawyer\n\n1. **Ask About Settlement vs. Litigation Mindset:** Over 90% of family law matters settle outside of court. Ensure your prospective lawyer prioritises Family Dispute Resolution (FDR) / mediation before jumping into court action.\n2. **Clarify Fee Structures:** Ask upfront whether they offer fixed-fee initial consultations, stage-by-stage billing, or require a trust retainer.\n3. **Check for Specialized Needs:** If your case involves complex tax issues, trusts, or company shares, ensure the firm has internal commercial expertise (like Bennett Carroll). If cultural/language barriers are present, firms like Denovo are usually better suited.",
